{
  "case": "due2-repeated-right-operand",
  "source": "due2-native: a set right operand written as an RDF list and as repeated values (decisions/0013)",
  "classification": "odrl-core",
  "needs": [],
  "notes": "Authored for due2; no origin result. ex:readListed and ex:readRepeated have the same constraint, written as odrl:rightOperand ( ex:EU ex:EEA ) and as odrl:rightOperand ex:EU, ex:EEA. Each scenario of one form has a twin in the other form, with the same expected answer: both forms give the right operand {ex:EU, ex:EEA} (due2-profiles.md §4). The repeated form is what the ODRL JSON-LD context makes of \"rightOperand\": [\"ex:EU\", \"ex:EEA\"]; rl2-multi-certification uses it with isAllOf. No warning is expected: isAnyOf is not one of the contested operators of decisions/0005.",
  "prefixes": {
    "ex": "https://example.org/"
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "list: region in the set",
      "request": {
        "reference": "req-1a",
        "action": "odrl:read",
        "target": "ex:ListedReport",
        "at": "2026-06-01T12:00:00Z",
        "parties": {
          "odrl:assignee": "ex:Dana"
        },
        "params": {}
      },
      "sotw": {
        "effective_at": "2026-06-01T12:00:00Z",
        "facts": {
          "ex:requesterRegion": {
            "status": "resolved",
            "values": [
              {
                "@id": "ex:EU"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "evidence": [],
        "activation": {},
        "closure": []
      },
      "expected": {
        "verdict": "Permit",
        "frontier": [],
        "obligations": [],
        "verdict_basis": [
          {
            "ref": "ex:readListed",
            "role": "permission"
          }
        ],
        "eliminated": [],
        "why": "The region ex:EU is one of {ex:EU, ex:EEA}, so isAnyOf is T and ex:readListed applies; nothing prohibits, so Permit."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "list: region outside the set",
